{
  "_about": "Provider universe for the Week 2 seller benchmark. Deliberately compact: CLAUDE.md's research posture makes provider messaging a comparative benchmark, not a co-equal research population, so this is sized to characterise the market Talbot West competes in rather than to enumerate it.",
  "_selection_rationale": "Chosen to span the three provider archetypes a mid-size industrial buyer actually encounters: (a) mid-market-focused management/technology consultancies, (b) accounting-firm consulting arms, which are disproportionately present in the private mid-market, and (c) systems integrators whose revenue comes from the ERP/supply-chain platforms these buyers run. Global tier-1 firms are represented but not over-weighted, because their mid-market practice is not what a 500-5,000 employee private company usually buys.",
  "_caveat": "Reliability ceiling is B per docs/signal_taxonomy.md SD-a: this is self-promotional content and inflated framing is expected. Observations from it describe what the provider MESSAGES about, never what the provider has demonstrably delivered.",
  "_page_kinds": "service = capability/solution page (what they sell). case = case study/client story (what they claim to have done).",

